<!-- ======================================================================== -->
<Section title="Methodology" subtitle="Sample design, coding, and statistical conventions">

<h3>Sample design</h3>

<p>Two-cohort B2B study designed to answer Intercom's Fin-on-Top strategic question. <strong>Wave 1 Fin Adopters (n={meta.n_wave_1_adopters})</strong>: companies that added Intercom Fin on top of an existing Zendesk or Salesforce Service Cloud helpdesk in the last 3-12 months, with Fin actively deployed. <strong>Wave 2 Non-Adopters (n={meta.n_wave_2_non_adopters})</strong>: companies on Zendesk or Salesforce Service Cloud, aware of Fin and aware that Fin can be deployed on top, who have not adopted Fin and have not actively deployed their platform's native AI agent.</p>

<p>Both cohorts: US-based, Director / VP / Head / CCO decision-makers in Customer Support, CX, or Customer Operations, 12+ months tenure in role, 5,000+ monthly support inquiries, 1,000-5,000 employees, in five qualifying industries (SaaS, Fintech, Ecommerce, Marketplaces, Digital Services). Hard quotas on platform (50/50 Zendesk/Salesforce) and industry (equal share). Wave 2 additionally has a hard size-band quota (50/50 1k-3k vs 3k-5k employees).</p>

<h3>Coding methodology</h3>

<p>Inductive thematic coding. Three-agent application pipeline: dual independent coders + arbiter resolution. Codebook: 55 codes, 7 thematic blocks. {me.n_segments_coded} segments coded across 24 questions × 180 participants.</p>

<table class="rec-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Reliability metric</th><th>Value</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Thematic-code Cohen's kappa</td><td>{me.thematic_kappa}</td><td>Almost perfect</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Codes below the reliability threshold</td><td>{me.n_codes_below_threshold} of {me.n_codes}</td><td>{me.n_codes_below_threshold === 0 ? "None (full codebook is reliable)" : "Listed below"}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Statistical methodology</h3>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Alpha:</strong> {me.alpha}, two-tailed. Not 0.05.</li>
  <li><strong>Default test:</strong> {me.test_default}.</li>
  <li><strong>Fallback:</strong> {me.test_fallback}.</li>
  <li><strong>Subgroup-vs-others convention:</strong> the dashed line on subgroup bar charts shows the overall sample average for visual reference, but the significance test compares the focal subgroup against all other respondents combined (subgroup excluded from the reference).</li>
  <li><strong>Three-tier claim discipline:</strong> only p &lt; 0.10 findings get directive recommendation language. Non-significant + corroborated claims get hedged ("directionally," "suggestive but not conclusive"). Non-significant + uncorroborated findings are not highlighted.</li>
</ul>

</Section>


